1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:01,921
I am trying to pay.

2
00:00:01,921 --> 00:00:05,474
I Tab to checkout’s last control and hear only “button.”

3
00:00:05,474 --> 00:00:07,152
What will it do?

4
00:00:07,152 --> 00:00:09,768
This is a screen reader simulation.

5
00:00:09,768 --> 00:00:12,499
The icon has no accessible name.

6
00:00:13,302 --> 00:00:20,088
I activate BarrierRelay at the focused button, describe what I
was trying to do, and select screen reader context.

7
00:00:20,088 --> 00:00:23,317
The optional trail records navigation keys.

8
00:00:23,317 --> 00:00:26,419
The extension hands off the capture locally.

9
00:00:26,419 --> 00:00:29,127
The screenshot stays in this browser.

10
00:00:32,436 --> 00:00:35,727
The app and Gemini Nano are already prepared.

11
00:00:35,727 --> 00:00:39,095
I go offline in DevTools and draft the report.

12
00:00:39,095 --> 00:00:42,856
Firebase AI Logic runs Nano on this device.

13
00:00:42,856 --> 00:00:47,058
The routing row shows on-device inference and zero cloud bytes.

14
00:00:47,058 --> 00:00:51,572
Local rules flag the unnamed button and can correct the
classification.

15
00:00:51,572 --> 00:00:53,898
Nano proposes a draft.

16
00:00:53,898 --> 00:00:57,706
I review it against the captured facts and run a self-check.

17
00:00:58,502 --> 00:01:01,955
I review the sharing controls and the approved JSON.

18
00:01:01,955 --> 00:01:05,415
Enabling the keyboard trail changes what would be sent.

19
00:01:05,415 --> 00:01:08,864
I leave it off, along with the coarse browser settings.

20
00:01:08,864 --> 00:01:11,700
The original note and image stay local.

21
00:01:11,700 --> 00:01:16,434
The approved payload contains redacted control facts and the
edited report.

22
00:01:16,434 --> 00:01:18,783
I can review it before sharing.

23
00:01:19,600 --> 00:01:22,590
Back online, I request a fix plan.

24
00:01:22,590 --> 00:01:28,331
Cloud Gemini uses URL context to retrieve W3C guidance for this
barrier.

25
00:01:28,331 --> 00:01:31,386
The byte count measures the approved payload.

26
00:01:31,386 --> 00:01:36,849
The plan includes suggested code, manual checks, and links to the
retrieved guidance.

27
00:01:37,650 --> 00:01:40,200
I share a real Firestore ticket.

28
00:01:40,200 --> 00:01:43,985
In the site owner desk, the owner acknowledges the report.

29
00:01:43,985 --> 00:01:45,929
Here is the source diff.

30
00:01:45,929 --> 00:01:50,235
The suggested code was applied to a demo copy of the checkout
page.

31
00:01:50,235 --> 00:01:53,718
The owner marks it fixed and asks me to re-capture.

32
00:01:53,718 --> 00:01:58,348
I reload the patched page, focus the same button, and capture it
again.

33
00:01:58,348 --> 00:02:01,716
The ticket verifies the repair with that re-capture.

34
00:02:01,716 --> 00:02:07,168
This checks one rule on this button; it does not establish WCAG
conformance.

35
00:02:07,988 --> 00:02:10,538
Browser code captures and checks.

36
00:02:10,538 --> 00:02:12,795
Nano drafts privately.

37
00:02:12,795 --> 00:02:15,850
Cloud Gemini adds guidance after approval.

38
00:02:15,850 --> 00:02:18,443
Firebase connects the workflow.

39
00:02:18,443 --> 00:02:21,452
Try BarrierRelay or explore the source.

40
00:02:21,452 --> 00:02:23,397
Report it privately.

41
00:02:23,397 --> 00:02:25,121
See it fixed.

